{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide","id":1474180,"title":"[Core] Talent Player's Guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-08T03:06:00-08:00","id":1474180,"title":"[Core] Talent Player's Guide","content":"Just a heads up on the new title which just appeared in the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-mage-mesa-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">Monday Meeting Notes</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T03:43:57-08:00","id":1474181,"title":"","content":"I saw that this morning and got pretty excited.<br /> <br /> Any general idea on what is it going to focus around or still too early to ask?<br /> <br /> I hope for some &quot;Talents over the ages&quot; and more about supertech. Also some about the weird stuff we see in Adventure and In Media Res but taken to the other settings, like weird places, esoteric stuff, dimention hopping and maybe just maybe time travel...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T04:17:39-08:00","id":1474185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474181#post1474181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any general idea on what is it going to focus around or still too early to ask?</div> </div> </div> </div>Still too early to ask. We've only just announced it, after all. More information will be coming soon, but until then, feel free to speculate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T05:03:29-08:00","id":1474188,"title":"","content":"Defo looking forward to it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T06:35:50-08:00","id":1474192,"title":"","content":"I hope it's an expansion of the masteries seen in Assassin's to other areas. A sourcebook about how to create specialized talents, if you will. Then expanded super science with clearer rules and more examples. Finally, an explanation of flux and how Talents can manipulate it more directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T08:49:12-08:00","id":1474201,"title":"","content":"I somehow doubt that it will focus on Masteries \u2014 ironically, this is because there's <i>too much to do</i> in that regard. <b>Assassins</b>, by itself, demonstrates that you can fill an entire book with <i>just one</i> specialized Talent. However, I certainly wouldn't mind some attention being given to that in the TPG; a sort of \u201cintroduction to other Masteries\u201d, if you will: something that lays the groundwork for further development of the idea, but which doesn't even <i>attempt</i> to be comprehensive. But personally, I'd rather more word count be devoted to Gifts than to Masteries. <br /> <br /> I do agree about revisiting and expanding on Super Science and the cross-time nature of Flux. On the Super Science side of things, I'd like to see <b>Aberrant</b>'s \u201creverse engineering\u201d concept adapted to the basic Super Science rules; and perhaps bring in something about how different Facets interact with Super Science: e.g., the Destructive Facet serving to amp up the effectiveness of Super Science while also resulting in more spectacular failures; the Intuitive Facet shortens the periodicity of the invention cycle; and the Reflective Facet reduces the chances of things going wrong (though when they <i>do</i> go wrong, I refer you to the suggestion regarding the Destructive Facet). <br /> <br /> More generally, I'd like to see the Facets reexamined to see if they need clarification and/or expansion on what they can do. <br /> <br /> And I'd also like to see Dramatic Editing get some review and expansion: at a <i>minimum</i>, bring in some of the DE innovations from <b>Assassins</b> as something available to <i>all</i> Talents \u2014 and possibly others, too: I'm thinking in particular of the \u201cexchange rate\u201d of two Momentum for one Inspiration in DE that <b>Assassins</b> introduced, which <i>could</i> also be expanded further to \u201c<i>anyone</i> with access to Momentum can engage in Dramatic Editing at these higher Momentum costs, even if they don't have Inspiration\u201d. I'm looking at novas, superiors, psions, and psiads in particular; but one the off-chance that someone wants to play a heroic <i>baseline</i> and is averse to calling them a Talent, this would apply here, too: basically, of it's a player character, the \u201cDramatic Editing for double Momentum\u201d rule would apply. <br /> <br /> And Facets might also factor into Dramatic Editing in some way, perhaps with Intuitive types getting some sort of edge with Dramatic Editing that involves serendipity, while Reflective types finding it easier to engage in Dramatic Editing that represents retroactive foresight, and Destructive types\u2026 well, I'd have to think about that one a bit more. <br /> <br /> Finally, it might be interesting to see some options for having <i>Paths</i> factor into Dramatic Editing: say, an optional rule where reach rank in a Path gives a Talent a specialized currency that can only be used to pay for Dramatic Editing in place of Inspiration points, and only if the player can explain how the Edit is justified by the Path. <br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> I also like Mateus Luz's suggestion of \u201cTalents through the ages\u201d: there's a \u201c22nd Century Talents\u201d supplement on the Nexus that addresses the issues with making Talents that use \u00c6on-era Paths (specifically, what Attributes and Skills are associated with each Origin, Role, and Society Path); and <i>at a minimum</i>, I'd want TPG to cover that, as well as their Aberrant-era counterparts that's aren't already covered in the TC core book. (Adventure! and Anima already prominently feature Talents, and ought to have already addressed these issues; but if they haven't, I'd address them here, too.) But I'd also like to see one or two era-tailored Gifts (either variants of existing Gifts that operate differently Ina given era, or new Gifts that are based on features unique to a given era), and maybe a box dedicated to summarizing TC:A!'s daredevil-style Dramatic Editing along with what conditions would need to be met in other eras to bring that back into play. <br /> <br /> (Personally, I'm inclined to bring daredevil-style DE into play in TC:Ab games, on the Doylean basis that Talents in a world dominated by superhumans need every edge they can get to stay relevant; and I'd justify it in Watsonian terms as a short-term byproduct of Divas Mal's Quantum Event: for the first couple of decades after the Galatea Explosion, daredevil-style Dramatic Editing is a thing again. But it needn't be limited to those two events: I could see, for example, a freak meteorite storm striking Kansas around the 1950s, resulting in a brief and local resurgence of the Adventure era. Think <b>Smallville</b>, but in the middle of the 20th century.)<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> So in summary: clarifications and expansions on the Paths, Facets, Dramatic Editing, Super Science, and Gifts from the core book; plus an introduction to non-<b>Assassins</b> Masteries, a closer look at Flux and how it relates to the Continuum, and guidelines for designing and playing Talents in other eras, specifically including Aberrant and \u00c6on.<br /> <br /> (But whatever you do, be very careful about mixing the expanded material on the Continuum with the \u201cTalents in other eras\u201d stuff; the last thing we need is another \u00c6on Flux incident.) :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T10:43:46-08:00","id":1474211,"title":"","content":"When I see this title I immediately think of 1e Aberrant Player's Guide (I really liked that book!). So one thing that I would expect from this book would be exploring the boundaries of talents. The very pinnacle of what they can potentially do. The alternate continuum where they are the dominant type. What do talents look like just before they ascend, how may they ascend? And some tips/meat on how to get there of course. The end game wasn't the whole book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24929-econclark","name":"econclark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T11:23:05-08:00","id":1474212,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, \u201cpinnacles of power\u201d was appropriate for the aberrant players guide because a major theme of apparent was and is the ascendance to power. That's not really a theme for Talents. That said, masteries are explicitly a step up from gifts, in that gifts are limited to stuff that is plausible while masteries are not. An example of a mastery from assassins involves being able to shoot around obstacles \u2014 that is, the trajectory of the bullet Benz around an obstacle. And I would argue that one reason why assassins has the shadow in it is because another theme of talents is that they don't seem to be superhuman. <br /> <br /> So when a talent has an ability that blatantly violates the laws of physics, like the aforementioned bullet bending, it only takes place behind a sort of masquerade, out of sight of the public. This would be one of the things that an introduction to non assassin masteries would address, in my view: what replaces the shadow? That said, one possible answer is \u201cnothing\u201d. Ozymandias from Watchmen could be considered an Assassin, in the sense that he has masteries; but the logic of the setting is such that those masteries may well be publicly known: with the exception of Dr Manhattan, The Watchmen universe could be said to be dominated by Talents; and ozymandias stands above even the other Talents in that his expertise allows him to do the impossible. In some flavors of the superhero genre, I could see running an aberrant game with talents being free to take and use masteries without having to hide in the Shadow. The earliest version of wonder woman, for example, where all of her incredible abilities came from Amazonian training, could be viewed as a talent with unconcealed masteries.<br /> <br /> But again, I don't think that should be the focus of the book. I can see it being something that the book deals with, to an extent; but that's not the same thing.<br /> <br /> I could also see the book explicitly dealing with cross time travel; but again, that wouldn't be the focus. And my inclination would be that it would be done via super science, as opposed to masteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T12:16:05-08:00","id":1474219,"title":"","content":"I think moving in the direction of &quot;Super Training&quot; to get to Wonder Woman style is a very solid approach for a non assassin mastery, it can be used to get to Mentats mental capacities.<br /> <br /> I honestly think the focus of the Talents must be Skills to super human levels, in opposition to Attributes to super human levels, basically you are capable of amazing things not because your natural capacities but because you trained beyond natural levels.<br /> <br /> I would say, like Stalwarts have attribute gifts and power gifts, talents may have Lucky Gifts (general luck), Skill Gifts (capacities beyond usual limitis) and Masteries (that are almost supernatural).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-08-2022, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T13:45:50-08:00","id":1474227,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised no one has hoped for Tier 3 Talent rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T16:50:30-08:00","id":1474239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474227#post1474227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised no one has hoped for Tier 3 Talent rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone did, we just don\u2019t talk about\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T20:34:32-08:00","id":1474252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474227#post1474227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised no one has hoped for Tier 3 Talent rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>My expectation is that the Nova and Proxy tier counterparts to Talents are a whole other type of being, not just a power advancement on Talents, so this is unlikely to be the place for them. Could be wrong though!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T04:54:08-08:00","id":1474279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474252#post1474252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My expectation is that the Nova and Proxy tier counterparts to Talents are a whole other type of being, not just a power advancement on Talents, so this is unlikely to be the place for them. Could be wrong though!</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you. While the consept is the same (a Talent that gets extremely powerful), the idea would be the same of a Stalwart and a Nova, the power behind is kind of the same, but the way it works is different enough to worth a different system.<br /> <br /> On a side note, a Proxy tier Psi user taken &quot;seriously&quot; (with a system to explore their full power without having to deal with lots of dice and a large number of psi points) would work different, basically they would work with Proxy Tier powers and free form lower level powers, working like Power Stunts, much like a Nova.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-09-2022, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T10:54:41-08:00","id":1474378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474252#post1474252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My expectation is that the Nova and Proxy tier counterparts to Talents are a whole other type of being, not just a power advancement on Talents, so this is unlikely to be the place for them. Could be wrong though!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not gonna lie, I'd very much like to see rules for Talents becoming...whatever you'd call the thing that Max Mercer is. We have rules for novas becoming outrageously powerful, and rules for psions becoming proxy-tier, so it would be nice for Talents to remain viable character options in &quot;high level&quot; games.<br /> <br /> I hope we'll see that in this book, but I don't really expect it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T12:20:24-08:00","id":1474384,"title":"","content":"Ditto. The official line is that Max is one of a kind; I suspect we're going to have to stick to STV products to get any peers for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T13:06:03-08:00","id":1474386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474384#post1474384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ditto. The official line is that Max is one of a kind; I suspect we're going to have to stick to STV products to get any peers for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>he\u2019s one of kind in the eras we\u2019ve seen, but I wouldn\u2019t rule out a far future rooted setting that incorporates other eras/timelines/settings by playing members of conflicting Allegiances of Mercer-style time hoppers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T16:33:08-08:00","id":1474400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474386#post1474386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> he\u2019s one of kind in the eras we\u2019ve seen, but I wouldn\u2019t rule out a far future rooted setting that incorporates other eras/timelines/settings by playing members of conflicting Allegiances of Mercer-style time hoppers!</div> </div> </div> </div>that's fine as any time manipulation powers are a massive headache for 99.9% of the population, and even then it usually just turns into Bill and Ted anyway,<br /> <br /> That said I'm pretty sure this is going to be offering expansions into the Tallent Type and guidance on how to play them across all the timelines and game lines. What I think would be cool is guidance on what happens when a Talent transcends the normal upper limits of a talent, kind of like how the proxies are technically a transcended form of the psions. The real question is how to go about gaining transcendence (not necessarily the nova kind), so far that is accomplished via outside force. The proxies by Q$%$%$#%#@@#$@, and the original batch by being at ground zero for the Hamerstone telueric engine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T17:06:32-08:00","id":1474401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474384#post1474384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ditto. The official line is that Max is one of a kind; I suspect we're going to have to stick to STV products to get any peers for him.</div> </div> </div> </div>...or is he","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T19:20:58-08:00","id":1474411,"title":"","content":"Truthfully, I think it would be very difficult to run a game with PCs who have exactly the same kind of wacky time powers as Mercer, but I do want it to be possible for PC Talents to become -- broadly speaking -- as powerful as he is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-10T22:03:59-08:00","id":1474415,"title":"","content":"I think that just some clarification to the Facets would help. As well as some better DE rules and examples would be great as I know my Talents seem to get stuck on what they can and cannot do. Superscience rules that cover how to give an item/formula/organism Gifts would be great. Also ways to possibly bring Mesmerist and Stalwarts Gifts to modern day or perhaps some setting specific Gifts would be awesome.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T00:22:52-08:00","id":1474419,"title":"","content":"If we take into account how time travel works as described in adventure, then it's not really as overpowered as it may seem. The characters have to be careful with ANY action they undertake, changes in the timeline must be subtle and small, otherwise they risk creating a mess of parallel timelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T02:29:28-08:00","id":1474422,"title":"","content":"You may say whatever you what, but I must say: Stalwarts and Mesmerists are not Talents and so they are not going to be in this book.<br /> This phrase pushes us into another question, are Assassins Talents or are they just another form of Flux users? Is Mercer a Talent or can we say he crossed the line to not be a talent anymore? It may seam a weird question, but we have Psiads and Psions and they work different, and Superiors and Novas are even more different, so...<br /> <br /> But I like the idea of Stalwart and Mesmerit gifts being brought up, as they are kind of leveled to talent gifts and they could fit amazingly well in a super science system. Imagine a Talent capable of inventing a Inspired Hardtech Varg, or a flight system, or a warp driver. I like the idea of a reality in the continuum where Psiads and Novas never come to be and Talents lead humanity to space exploration and all other options we see in the sci fi genre, with out powers but with super tech in their hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T02:33:18-08:00","id":1474423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474378#post1474378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> so it would be nice for Talents to remain viable character options in &quot;high level&quot; games.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Since the core effects of Talents basically bend the &quot;plot&quot; of the world to their desires, higher-level Talents are probably terrifying. <br /> <br /> It's the comic-book effect of the random &quot;highly-skilled human&quot; who manages to take on world-shaking monstrosities and then, amazingly, win. All the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T03:20:51-08:00","id":1474424,"title":"","content":"It would be Edge Of Tomorrow style of game, you die and do it again until master it to an absurd level. You know what to do, when to do and how to do it in the &quot;bestest&quot; way.<br /> <br /> The only difference is that you jump the infinite number of tries and go straight to the best result possible, that is basically how the rest of the world see the result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T12:10:02-08:00","id":1474434,"title":"","content":"I always get a stormer ala TORG vibe from how talents are described, where they manipulate possibilities to pull off a better outcome. How ever once they develop thier powers they start pulling off outrageous things that start veering into interdimensional foam Manipulation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T15:14:28-08:00","id":1474445,"title":"","content":"I always picture a tier 3 talent as someone with access to the time stone of Doctor Strange. They can literally see, and live, through millions of possible futures in less than a second and know the exact sequence of events and dramatic editing they need to get the future they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T19:55:09-08:00","id":1474471,"title":"","content":"There is so much focus on time. But there are also other things. For example, there are Gifts which allow you have vast social abilities. Or else things that give you awareness beyond normal senses. So, those could also be expanded upon more than just time manipulation like most people seem fixated on. Yes, Mercer has some time travel powers because he is the most powerful Talent that has been documented but then you have Divis Mal who can manipulate plasma. So, are the most powerful Novas suppose to have some ties to plasma? No. They have a wide array of possibilities. So let's start the speculation on things other than time for high tier Talents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T21:46:51-08:00","id":1474702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474445#post1474445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always picture a tier 3 talent as someone with access to the time stone of Doctor Strange. They can literally see, and live, through millions of possible futures in less than a second and know the exact sequence of events and dramatic editing they need to get the future they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can see that working very well...<br /> <img src=\"https://comicvine.gamespot.com/a/uploads/original/11/116790/2245176-untitled_scanned_23__2__2.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-14T21:56:18-08:00","id":1474704,"title":"","content":"Or <a href=\"https://larryniven.fandom.com/wiki/Teela_Brown\" target=\"_blank\">Teela Brown</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T05:29:38-08:00","id":1474724,"title":"","content":"Midnighter is prety much a Nova with almost all Mega Attributes in low levels and an amazing gift for fighting.<br /> <br /> OR he is a Assassin/Talent with superhuman training that let him operate in higher scale VERY often and effortless (Saitama / old Wonder Woman / Itadori pr\u00e9-Sukuna finger eating)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-15-2022, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T18:31:36-08:00","id":1474768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474724#post1474724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Midnighter is prety much a Nova with almost all Mega Attributes in low levels and an amazing gift for fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, on the table, I would 100% run him using the nova rules. Almost exactly as you describe with a variety of Mega-Edges to round out his abilities and maybe Boost to get them where they need to be on the fly. <br /> <br /> Lorewise, I don't think there is a box that suits his abilities, powers, &amp; origin story in the Trinity Continuum (at least, not as a player character, as an antagonist with Primary/Secondary/Desperation pools - pretty much anything goes). Bioware just doesn't have the &quot;oomph&quot; to do what Midnighter is capable of and, given he is a normal man without the enhancements (established both in his origins and several times where they turn them off on him), he's not a nova powering Q-tech. None of which is a slight on the TC rules - they are designed for a given setting and work well in it. I haven't yet seen the Assassins stuff, so I may be wrong about this, but Talent abilities/powers tend stay in the realms of <i>&quot;incredible but vaguely plausible&quot;</i> and Midnighter is well beyond that.<br /> <br /> Sorry, babbling a little. The Authority is one of the most influential works on my view of super-hero modern mythology. Wish I could respect the man behind the work as much as I do the work itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-15T22:44:45-08:00","id":1474787,"title":"","content":"Agree with you in all you described, and usually it\u2019s in the side of \u201cwe can\u2019t say he is a nova because it\u2019s not a quantum power\u201d. In reality no super hero is a Nova, maybe with exception of Dr Manhattan, but questionable, so I agree most of the job must be done without going to the real source of power.<br /> <br /> It would be possible to try by creating a bunch of Nova tech biological alterations and adding it to a regular man (in this case he would be a talent, because normal people that have a protagonist role in TC is at least a talent). It may work as expected, but it would be hard to balance because it would require like a dozen independent items\u2026 but he would not be unique if it was sample\u2026<br /> <br /> The Authority is just awesome\u2026 its impossible to describe properly\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T20:35:08-07:00","id":1489386,"title":"","content":"How is it coming along?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26322-ryu238","name":"ryu238","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T22:25:19-07:00","id":1489391,"title":"","content":"I would very like much have a section on 'Talents as magic users' expanded on. In Aether and Adventure! there is pointed notion of some characters still thinking they have MAGIC - not Super Science - as their power source. I'm really interested how this would come to Talents variants. Mesmerists are simple in interpretation -'You are wizard/psion'. Novas are somehow too - ' You are demigod, blessed by gods'. ( I would also be not shocked it's general theme of coming Aegis era.)<br /> <br /> With 'Talents as magic users' I have some mental block to envision this... \ud83d\ude14","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-07-2022, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T23:27:59-07:00","id":1489393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ryu238</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1489386#post1489386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is it coming along?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Production status of all our projects can be found in the monthly Release Roundup blog.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/release-roundup-july-2022/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/release-roundup-july-2022/\" target=\"_blank\"> Release Roundup: July 2022 &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/release-roundup-july-2022/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/release-roundup-july-2022/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T12:57:51-07:00","id":1489666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1474401#post1474401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...or is he</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He is at least *two* of his kind, if we count his dark self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1524-pcontop","name":"pcontop","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1524_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T13:08:42-07:00","id":1489667,"title":"","content":"I think at this point we can say Max is a Magog that has no Magog gifts. Maybe he is even more special and can access Luck and Skill gifts, But so far we do have some of his powers in the Gog and Magog gift list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T14:01:32-07:00","id":1489674,"title":"","content":"\u201cHe's a Magog with no Magog Gifts\u2026 some of his powers appear as Magog Gifts\u201d strikes me as a contradiction. <br /> <br /> I'm waiting until next Tuesday to see what the Setting Secrets for \u00c6ther are before I make up my mind on this; but right now, I'm leaving against Max being a Magog. <br /> <br /> I've been a proponent of their being \u201cmore like Max\u201d for a long time (my post to the contrary on the first page of this thread was motivated by the understanding at the time that the official line was that their aren't; but if Ian says that may not be the case, I won't argue). But my gut reaction to the idea of \u201cMax is the Last \u00c6thernaut, not an advanced Talent\u201d is\u2026 uneasiness. Again, my mind might change once the \u00c6ther Setting Secrets are out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T14:09:32-07:00","id":1489676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1489667#post1489667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think at this point we can say Max is a Magog that has no Magog gifts. Maybe he is even more special and can access Luck and Skill gifts, But so far we do have some of his powers in the Gog and Magog gift list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think Max is a Magog? He doesn\u2019t seem very inhuman to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T14:24:09-07:00","id":1489679,"title":"","content":"I think he <i>meant</i> \u201ca Magog without any Deviations\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T18:44:13-07:00","id":1489698,"title":"","content":"A Magog Gift has the Magog tag, but not all gifts of the Magog list are Magog gifts.<br /> <br /> Basically a Magog can pick any gift with the Attribute keyword and any gift with the Magog keyword. If it has the Magog keyword you must have a Deviation with it, otherwise it has no additional impact.<br /> <br /> So Max has gifts that are in the available list of Magogs (but not talents) that don\u2019t have the Magog keyword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T19:03:57-07:00","id":1489701,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, Squires can take those, too. The only gifts that Squires cannot take are the ones explicitly marked Gog or Magog.<br /> <br /> Basically, there are four kinds of gifts in this game. First there are those that are available only to squires. These are the luck gifts. Second, there are those that are available only to Gogs. These are the Gog Gifts, and require you to have apparatus. Third there are those that are only available to Magogs. These are the Magog Gifts, and require you to take deviations. Fourth there are gifts that are available to all three. These are all other gifts. I'll accept the luck gifts are aptitude gifts, and are split between attribute and skill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-10-2022, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T19:54:15-07:00","id":1489707,"title":"","content":"Actually there are 7 combinations of keywords that affect who can have it or not:<br /> Luck: only Squire<br /> Atribute: Squire and Magog<br /> Skill: Squire and Gog<br /> Atribute + Gog: Gog and Magog<br /> Atribute + Magog: Only Magog<br /> Skill + Magog: Gog and Magog<br /> Skill + Gog: Only Gog<br /> <br /> All gifts a Gog have need an apparatus, having or not the gog keyword.<br /> Magogs have a deviation for each Gift with the Magog tag they have.<br /> <br /> Max, as I see, would have the Accelerate Tempo, that is Attribute (Cunning) + Gog, meaning Squires can\u2019t have (for the Gog keyword), Magogs can have with no deviation (as it\u2019s an Attribute gift, but not a Magog one) and Gogs can have (as it\u2019s a Gog gift).<br /> <br /> Edit: there is a correction pointed in the discord that Magogs can have Gog gifts with no Magog keyword if it\u2019s an attribute gift, and Gogs can have Magog gifts with no Gog keyword if it\u2019s an skill gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 08-10-2022, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T20:24:16-07:00","id":1489711,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes: the leftover gifts that Gogs have from their time as Magogs, or the leftover gifts that Magogs have from their time as Gogs. As I understand it, it is impossible to be a Magog without any Magog Gifts, as you don't stop being a Gog until you pick one up. And vice versa. <br /> <br /> I could see Gogs and Magogs as prototypes of what Talents have the potential to become under the right circumstances; and if so, I could see \u201cadvanced Talents\u201d having Gog and Magog Gifts. <br /> <br /> That said, I'm sticking to my earlier assertion: I'm not committing to anything until the Setting Secrets are out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" targ