 not a Magog one) and Gogs can have (as it\u2019s a Gog gift).<br /> <br /> Edit: there is a correction pointed in the discord that Magogs can have Gog gifts with no Magog keyword if it\u2019s an attribute gift, and Gogs can have Magog gifts with no Gog keyword if it\u2019s an skill gift.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gosh this is complicated lol. I thought Storyteller and Storypath games were supposed to be rules-light, at least compared to games like D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T07:51:02-07:00","id":1489743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1474180-core-talent-player-s-guide?p=1489667#post1489667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think at this point we can say Max is a Magog that has no Magog gifts. Maybe he is even more special and can access Luck and Skill gifts, But so far we do have some of his powers in the Gog and Magog gift list.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Squires, Gogs, and Magogs are from <b>Aether</b>.<br /> <br /> Max developed powers in the Hammersmith explosion.<br /> <br /> This is a thread about the Talent Players Guide for the TC core. If 